(((
Ex 4: a novella in eight chapters, written to test Inquests. A draft for
Inkjot v0.6: it uses `state`, `~ id`, `~ inquest`, `~ inquest for`,
`~ inquest by monkeypaw ~ rejoin`, `pending:`, `theme` and the analysis
tags on Links (`~ beat`, `~ weighs`, `~ arc`, `~ stakes`, `~ plants`,
`~ pays off`, `~ predict`, `~ lasting`), none of which `inkjot check` 0.5
accepts. Analysis tags never change play; the engine passes them to the
IR for the Inker's reports.

Every chapter ends on a decision readers will argue about. The canon Link
is plain; the Inker's alternative sits just below it, hidden, marked
`~ inquest`. A Linker who presses Inquest writes what they wanted first,
then sees the forks flip in place (flow D). Three Inquests a reading.

Chapter One is Mark's first draft of Darklands: Winter 1, unchanged. The
rest is an imagined novella grown from it, not the real book.
)))
